{"severity":"error","file":"errors/linear_generic_param_4.march","start_line":13,"start_col":35,"end_line":13,"end_col":36,"message":"This passes `g` a value that may be linear: the enclosing function opted in to linear values of its type (`linear x : ...`), but `g` is generic in a parameter of that type, so it may drop or duplicate the value.\nConsume the value here instead, or, if `g` uses that parameter exactly once, mark it `linear` where `g` is defined.","code":"linear_generic_param","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[]}
